nt Awards Convocation; verify the current ceremony’s venue and attendance guidance.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"depauw-meet-at-the-boulder","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Meeting at the Columbian Boulder","title":"Meet at the Campus’s Giant Granite Marker","subtitle":"A gathering custom on the East College lawn","notes":"Use the inscribed Boulder as a daylight meeting point and examine it from the lawn; avoid the unsafe, clothing-optional run in older lore.","short_summary":"A granite curiosity delivered by 26 horses became a long-running campus rendezvous point.","evidence_claim":"The Columbian Boulder has served as an iconic student gathering place, and DePauw’s archives document its earlier use as a meeting point for chapel dates.","source_url":"https://library.depauw.edu/library/archives/ehistory/chapter2/symbols.html","source_title":"Symbols of Old DePauw","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Viewable outdoors on the East College lawn; this card covers the safe gathering custom and explicitly excludes the Boulder Run.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"depauw-baccalaureate-celebration","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Baccalaureate Celebration","title":"Begin Commencement With Many Traditions","subtitle":"DePauw’s formal ceremony before graduation day","notes":"Arrive before the listed start to hear student reflections, music, prayers and readings that open DePauw’s commencement weekend.","short_summary":"Graduation weekend formally begins with a multi-tradition gathering centered on the senior class.","evidence_claim":"DePauw describes Baccalaureate as the first formal event of Commencement Weekend, featuring the president, student reflections, music, prayers and readings from many traditions.","source_url":"https://www.depauw.edu/academics/academic-resourc